    "created_at": "2021-08-03T16:08:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-08-03T16:08:50Z",
    "body": "Note that it's not clear implementations actually do this for `WebSocket` et al. They might just keep the object alive for the duration of the connection instead (or lifetime of the document, whichever is shorter). So this might not end up depending so much on `EventTarget`, but rather upon document lifetime and whatever I/O the object is responsible for.",
